# Railway Deployment Environment Variables
# Copy these to your Railway project's environment variables section

# ===== REQUIRED VARIABLES =====
# These MUST be set for the application to work

# Supabase Configuration
# Get these from: https://app.supabase.com/project/_/settings/api
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ===== OPTIONAL VARIABLES =====
# These can be left empty - features will be disabled

# Supabase Admin (for admin dashboard and bulk operations)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# AI Enrichment (disabled by default in code)
# Only set if you want to enable AI-powered product enrichment
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OR (not both)
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ===== PLATFORM VARIABLES =====
# These are automatically set by Railway - DO NOT SET MANUALLY

# NODE_ENV=production
# PORT=3000
# RAILWAY_STATIC_URL=<auto-populated>
# RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN=<auto-populated>

# ===== INSTRUCTIONS =====
# 1. Create a Supabase project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Copy your Project URL to NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
# 3. Copy your anon/public key to NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# 4. (Optional) Add service role key for admin features
# 5. (Optional) Add AI API keys if you want enrichment
# 6. Deploy to Railway - that's it!

# ===== COST PROTECTION =====
# This deployment is configured with automatic cost protection:
# - Minimal resource allocation (512MB RAM, 0.5 CPU)
# - Free tier monitoring
# - Auto-shutdown if limits exceeded
# - Maintenance page deployment on shutdown
# See railway.toml for full configuration

# ===== FEATURE FLAGS =====
# AI enrichment is DISABLED by default (no API key needed)
# To enable: Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY and update:
# app/submit/action.ts: aiEnrichmentEnabled = true
